 "notes": "Daily-timeframe NIFTY futures long/short mean reversion and pullback-in-trend, train 2023-01-01..2024-12-31, 1 lot, default costs. All specs: timeframe 1d, signal entry acted next day 09:20, monthly future (min_days 2), swing max_days 10, check 15m, underlying ATR(14,1d) stop. Families tried: RSI(2)/RSI(3) Connors with SMA200 filter (exits close>SMA5 / RSI2>70 / close>SMA10, ATR 2 and 3); z-score(10/20) at -1/-1.5/-2; Bollinger %B<0; Williams %R(14)<-90; IBS (Williams %R(1)); 3 down days; RSI14<40 pullback in EMA50>SMA200 trend; EMA20 pullback with ADX>20; stochastic K<10; CCI<-150; percent_rank<10; short mirrors (RSI2>90, z>1.5). Findings: the exit matters more than the entry - RSI2>70 exit beat close>SMA5 on every entry. Deeper dips (z20<-1.5, %B<0, CCI<-150) worked; shallow / frequent signals (IBS, 3 down days, Williams %R14, classic close>SMA5 Connors exit) lost. Short side lost in 2023 (drift) and won only in 2024 - not submitted. EMA20/ADX pullback lost. z family is smooth across neighbours (z10/z20 x -1/-1.5/-2 all positive overall; exits rsi2>60/70/80, z>0 all positive); but z20<-1.5 was the best cell, so expect decay. The ATR 3 stop never fired on z20 (identical to ATR 5); it is protective only. Caveats: only ~20 trades in 2 years, daily t 1.5 ungated (test rule needs t>=2 - likely to fail on t even if the edge persists); 2023 was weak in points (+410 pts over 8 trades vs +3098 over 11 in 2024), 2024H1 carries 2/3 of the money. Gate regime!=3 was chosen post hoc among 6 gates tried (vix>13, vix<13, vix>VIX SMA20, regime!=3, close>SMA200, ADX<25); vix>VIX-SMA20 was second (+120k, t 1.92). Other variants: max_days 5 gave +132k t 1.73; 2x slippage costs only -1.6k. SENSEX replication only possible for 2024H2 (futures sparse): 6 trades +30k, 26 skipped.",
